Letter Mail Controlled 8/31/2009 10:34:54 AM MC# 2090543: - From J. Randolph Babbitt, Administrator: 09  The FAA has developed and published a number of initiatives to address decision making skills and flight risk evaluation programs for HEMS operators. 
January 28, 2005, the FAA published Notice 8000.293, Helicopter Emergency Medical Services Operations, providing guidance for safety inspectors to help operators review pilot and mechanic decision-making skills, procedural adherence, and crew resource management practices (concepts now found in Safety Alert for Operators 06001); 
August 1, 2005, the FAA published Notice 8000.301, Operational Risk Assessment Programs for Helicopter Emergency Medical Services (previously provided) providing guidance to inspectors promoting improved risk assessment, risk management tools and training to all flight crews, including medical staff; 
January 28, 2006, the FAA published Safety Alert for Operators 06001, Helicopter Emergency Medical Services Operations, which included the information from these Notices as well as additional information to operators (enclosure 3); and 
May 1, 2008, the FAA incorporated the risk assessment information into FAA Order 8900.1, FSIMS (enclosures 4 & 5). 
After several FAA and HEMS industry meetings, the industry has agreed to voluntarily implement risk assessment programs. As of February 2009, the industry had a 94 percent compliance with this agreement. In lieu of an OpSpec, as indicated in our initial response, the FAA is pursuing rulemaking to ensure 100 percent compliance. We plan to complete work on the NPRM for air ambulance and commercial helicopter operations in January 2010. Publication of the NPRM will occur after clearance from DOT and OMB.

